<h3>About VALE OER Collaborative Projects</h3>
<p>The VALE OER Collaborative Projects Collection houses the OER developed through the VALE-NJ OER Certificate Program launched in Summer 2022. This 5-week online course is designed to introduce librarians and library staff across the VALE-NJ network to open educational resources (OER) and engage them in the development of collaborative, multi-institutional solutions to increase the use and application of OER across colleges and universities within New Jersey. This course aims to:

Advance participants’ knowledge of OER, Creative Commons, and open pedagogy

Build competencies for advancing participants’ own OER institutional needs

Connect participants with colleagues across NJ to foster institutional collaborations.

For more information, please see https://vale.njedge.net/initiatives-services/oer-open-educational-resources/.</p>
